1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,163
AI agents are starting to spend company money:

2
00:00:04,213 --> 00:00:06,631
software, suppliers, refunds.

3
00:00:06,681 --> 00:00:09,693
So every CFO asks the same question:

4
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:11,650
who is holding the pen?

5
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:14,948
Give an agent a card number and

6
00:00:14,998 --> 00:00:18,168
hope, or approve every cent yourself.

7
00:00:18,218 --> 00:00:21,213
One is a risk no auditor signs off.

8
00:00:21,263 --> 00:00:23,650
The other saves you nothing.

9
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:28,499
Purser gives every AI agent its own company card and

10
00:00:28,549 --> 00:00:33,074
its own on-chain mandate, with limits the CFO sets once.

11
00:00:33,124 --> 00:00:37,650
Anything above those limits waits for the CFO's Face ID.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,162
Watch. The sourcing agent buys software:

13
00:00:41,212 --> 00:00:42,763
approved by Airwallex.

14
00:00:42,813 --> 00:00:47,130
Then the Pro plan, forty-five euros, on a thirty euro limit:

15
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:49,314
declined, by Airwallex itself.

16
00:00:49,364 --> 00:00:51,061
The agent asks for more.

17
00:00:51,111 --> 00:00:55,210
The CFO checks the exact terms and approves with Face ID.

18
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:59,650
The limit moves to fifty, and the same purchase goes through.

19
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,947
A euro invoice arrives:

20
00:01:01,997 --> 00:01:03,940
eighteen hundred and fifty.

21
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:08,146
The treasury agent checks the reserve, takes a live quote

22
00:01:08,196 --> 00:01:12,278
and converts only the missing three hundred and seventy.

23
00:01:12,328 --> 00:01:15,082
One Face ID covers the rate, the payee

24
00:01:15,132 --> 00:01:17,149
and the most the fee may be.

25
00:01:17,199 --> 00:01:19,436
Airwallex sends it by SWIFT; in

26
00:01:19,486 --> 00:01:21,650
the sandbox it is marked paid.

27
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,190
On Metal, agents pay per request, cents at

28
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:28,130
a time, under mandates that live on chain.

29
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:30,930
When the supplier doubles its price, the

30
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:33,940
payment hits the mandate's cap and bounces:

31
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:37,230
nothing moves, and the customer is not charged.

32
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:40,940
Purser prices two options, Opus reviews them, the CFO

33
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:44,440
signs one, and the mandates are replaced on chain.

34
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:48,640
Mandates, x402, signed orders and payouts ran here; clearing

35
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:51,650
and a receive policy in separate live runs.

36
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:55,861
Then our simulated customer disputes twelve orders:

37
00:01:55,911 --> 00:01:59,259
our agent never ordered this, refund everything.

38
00:01:59,309 --> 00:02:02,233
Northwind's Dispute desk checks the proof:

39
00:02:02,283 --> 00:02:05,065
every order signed by their agent, every

40
00:02:05,115 --> 00:02:07,756
payment inside their mandate on chain.

41
00:02:07,806 --> 00:02:08,959
Twelve of twelve.

42
00:02:09,009 --> 00:02:11,650
Claim rejected; nothing more refunded.

43
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:13,764
Need something once?

44
00:02:13,814 --> 00:02:18,912
Ask Purser: a flight to Berlin, at most one hundred and fifty euros.

45
00:02:18,962 --> 00:02:21,562
Airwallex issues a single-use card.

46
00:02:21,612 --> 00:02:25,650
The booking goes through; a second charge is declined.

47
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,538
Claude agents read, plan and advise;

48
00:02:28,588 --> 00:02:31,017
Metal and Airwallex enforce the limits.

49
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:33,878
Thirty-nine red-team attacks in a test world:

50
00:02:33,928 --> 00:02:36,293
all failed, two found only afterwards.

51
00:02:36,343 --> 00:02:39,980
Optional four eyes, an emergency stop tested on stand-ins,

52
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:42,650
about nine cents of AI per thousand euros.

53
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:49,934
Purser. Agents move at machine speed, and the CFO keeps the pen.

54
00:02:49,984 --> 00:02:52,650
Every payment has a proof.
